#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>char</command><arg>identifier</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This command allows you to insert literal characters by their numerical "
"identifier, in decimal, octal or hexadecimal form. To use it launch the "
"Editing Command dialog and type <userinput>char: [number]</userinput> in the "
"entry box, then hit <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>char</command> examples"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "Input: <userinput>char:234</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "Output: <computeroutput>&#234;</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "Input: <userinput>char:0x1234</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "Output: <computeroutput>&#x1234;</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: advanced.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid "replace, sed style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: advanced.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "search, sed style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: advanced.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>s///[ig]</command> <command>%s///[ig]</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This command does a sed-like search/replace operation on the current line, "
"or on the whole file (<command>%s///</command>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In short, the text is searched for text matching the <emphasis>search "
"pattern</emphasis>, the regular expression between the first and the second "
"slash, and when a match is found, the matching part of the text is replaced "
"with the expression between the middle and last part of the string. "
"Parentheses in the search pattern create <emphasis>back references</"
"emphasis>, that is the command remembers which part of the match matched in "
"the parentheses; these strings can be reused in the replace pattern, "
"referred to as <userinput>\\1</userinput> for the first set of parentheses, "
"<userinput>\\2</userinput> for the second and so on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To search for a literal <literal>(</literal> or <literal>)</literal>, you "
"need to <emphasis>escape</emphasis> it using a backslash character: "
"<userinput>\\(\\)</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you put an <userinput>i</userinput> at the end of the expression, the "
"matching will be case insensitive. If you put a <userinput>g</userinput> at "
"the end, all occurrences of the pattern will be replaced, otherwise only the "
"first occurrence is replaced."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replacing text in the current line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your friendly compiler just stopped, telling you that the class "
"<classname>myClass</classname> mentioned in line 3902 in your source file is "
"not defined."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:427
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&quot;Buckle!&quot; you think, it is of course <classname>MyClass</"
"classname>. You go to line 3902, and instead of trying to find the word in "
"the text, you launch the Editing Command Dialog, enter <userinput>s/myclass/"
"MyClass/i</userinput>, hit the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button, save the "
"file and compile &ndash; successfully without the error."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replacing text in the whole file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Imagine that you have a file, in which you mention a <quote>Miss Jensen</"
"quote> several times, when someone comes in and tells you that she just got "
"married to <quote>Mr Jones</quote>. You want, of course, to replace each and "
"every occurrence of <quote>Miss Jensen</quote> with <quote>Ms Jones</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the command line and issue the command <userinput>%s/Miss Jensen/Ms "
"Jones/</userinput> and hit return, you are done."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid "A More Advanced Example"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This example makes use of <emphasis>back references</emphasis> as well as a "
"<emphasis>character class</emphasis> (if you do not know what that is, "
"please refer to the related documentation mentioned below)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "Suppose you have the following line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: advanced.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"void MyClass::DoStringOps( String      &amp;foo, String &amp;bar String *p, "
"int  &amp;a, int &amp;b )"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you realize that this is not nice code, and decide that you want to use "
"the <constant>const</constant> keyword for all <quote>address of</quote> "
"arguments, those characterized by the &amp; operator in front of the "
"argument name. You would also like to simplify the white space, so that "
"there is only 1 whitespace character between each word."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Launch the Editing Command Dialog, and enter: <userinput>s/\\s+(\\w+)\\s"
"+(&amp;)/ const \\1 \\2/g</userinput> and hit the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> "
"button. The <userinput>g</userinput> at the end of the expression makes the "
"regular expression recompile for each match to save the "
"<emphasis>backreferences</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Output: <computeroutput>void MyClass::DoStringOps( const String &amp;foo, "
"const String &amp;bar String *p, const int &amp;a, const int &amp;b )</"
"computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Mission completed! Now, what happened? Well, we looked for some white space "
"(<literal>\\s+</literal>) followed by one or more alphabetic characters "
"(<literal>\\w+</literal>) followed by some more whitespace (<literal>\\s+</"
"literal>) followed by an ampersand, and in the process saved the alphabetic "
"chunk and the ampersand for reuse in the replace operation. Then we replaced "
"the matching part of our line with one whitespace followed by <quote>const</"
"quote> followed by one whitespace followed by our saved alphabetical chunk "
"(<literal>\\1</literal>) followed by one whitespace followed by our saved "
"ampersand (<literal>\\2</literal>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now in some cases the alphabetical chunk was <quote>String</quote>, in some "
"<quote>int</quote>, so using the character class <literal>\\w</literal> and "
"the <literal>+</literal> quantifier proved a valuable asset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands for navigation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>goto</command><arg>INT line</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid "This command navigates to the specified line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:516
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>find</command><arg>pattern</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This command navigates to the first occurrence of <userinput>pattern</"
"userinput> according to the configuration. Following occurrences can be "
"found using <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find Next</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> (the default shortcut is <keycap>F3</keycap>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:522
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The find command can be configured by appending a colon followed by one or "
"more options, the form is <userinput>find:options pattern</userinput>. The "
"following options are supported:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:570
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>ifind</command><arg>pattern</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This command provides <quote>as-you-type</quote> searching. You can "
"configure the behavior of the search by appending a colon followed by one or "
"more options, like this: <userinput>ifind:options pattern</userinput>. "
"Allowed options are"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid "Do regular expression search."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:610
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Code Folding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:612
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Code folding allows you to hide parts of a document in the editor, making it "
"easier to overview large documents. In &kate; the foldable regions are "
"calculated using rules defined in the syntax highlight definitions, and "
"therefore it is only available in some formats - typically program source "
"code, XML markup and similar. Most highlight definitions supporting code "
"folding also lets you manually define foldable regions, typically using the "
"<userinput>BEGIN</userinput> and <userinput>END</userinput> keywords."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use the code folding feature, activate the folding markers using "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Folding Markers</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item if they are not already visible. The "
"Folding Markers Pane in the left side of the screen displays a graphical "
"view of the foldable regions, with +/- signs to indicate the possible "
"operation on a given region: a - means that the region is expanded, clicking "
"the - will collapse the region and a + will be displayed instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:628
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Four commands are provided to manipulate the state of folding regions, see "
"the <link linkend=\"view-code-folding\">menu documentation</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you do not want to use the code folding feature, you can disable the "
"<guilabel>Show folding markers (if available)</guilabel> option in the <link "
"linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-appearance\">Appearance page of the editor "
"configuration</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scripting the editor component with Javascript"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:645
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Starting with version 2.5, the &kate; editor component supports scripting "
"with ECMA script, also known as JavaScript."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:650
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Scripts can be used through <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-tools-"
"commandline\">the built-in command line</link> only. The requirement is that "
"the script is placed in a folder where &kate; can find it, along with an "
"optional .desktop file that defines the related properties. The valid folder "
"are named <filename>katepart/scripts</filename> in the &kde; data folders. "
"You can find the data folders by running the command <command>kde4-config "
"<option>--path</option> <parameter>data</parameter></command> You will "
"usually have at least a system and a personal data folder. Of course scripts "
"in the system data folder are available to all users on the system, while "
"those in the personal folder are only available for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:661
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This feature is experimental and will most likely change during future "
"development."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:663
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We know that many of you will be disappointed because you can't add your "
"scripts to the menu or assign shortcuts to them. Sorry, sometime in the "
"future that will likely be possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:666
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is also not possible to pass any arguments to your scripts yet. Be "
"patient, and that may be added in the bright future ;)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:674
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Kate JavaScript API"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:676
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here is listed the complete set of functions and properties available in the "
"<type>document</type> and <type>view</type> objects. In addition you can of "
"course use all the standard objects such as <type>Math</type>, <type>String</"
"type> <type>Regex</type> and so forth."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:681
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a script is run, the <classname>document</classname> object is the "
"current document, and the <classname>view</classname> object is the current "
"view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:685
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The types of arguments are of course not used in JavaScript at this time, "
"they are there solely to indicate what sort of value the funcitons expect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:690
#, no-c-format
msgid "Global Functions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:692
#, no-c-format
msgid "debug( <parameter><replaceable>string</replaceable></parameter>) [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:696
#, no-c-format
msgid "parameters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:697
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>string</parameter> the string to output"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:700
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Outputs the string to <acronym>STDERR</acronym> using <function>kDebug()</"
"function>. A dedicated output area is used for the output, which will be "
"prefixed <computeroutput>Kate (KJS Scripts):</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:709
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <classname>document</classname> API"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:712
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"document.attribute( <parameter><replaceable>line</replaceable> </parameter>, "
"<parameter><replaceable>column</replaceable></parameter> ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:717 advanced.docbook:736 advanced.docbook:752
#: advanced.docbook:778 advanced.docbook:793 advanced.docbook:808
#: advanced.docbook:866 advanced.docbook:882 advanced.docbook:920
#: advanced.docbook:933 advanced.docbook:955 advanced.docbook:983
#: advanced.docbook:996 advanced.docbook:1107 advanced.docbook:1126
#: advanced.docbook:1145
#, no-c-format
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "Paramètres"

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:718
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>uint line</parameter> The line of the position for which to find "
"the attribute."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>uint column</parameter> The column of the position for which to "
"find the attribute."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:723
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the numeric ID of the attribute for the document position "
"[<parameter>line</parameter>,<parameter>column</parameter>]. The attribute "
"represents the visual appearance or style of the text, and is also used to "
"calculate the syntax highlight for a specific part of the text in mixed "
"formats like HTML or PHP."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:732
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"document.canBreakAt( <parameter>Char c</parameter>, <parameter>uint "
"attribute</parameter> ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:737
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>c</parameter> The character to test"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:738
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>attribute</parameter> The attribute at the position of "
"<parameter>c</parameter>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:741
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns whether it is allowed to break the line at a character c with "
"attribute attribute. The result is decided by querying the highlight owning "
"attribute for which characters allow breaking the line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:748
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"document.canComment( <parameter>uint start_attribute</parameter>, "
"<parameter>uint end_attribute</parameter> ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:753
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>start_attribute</parameter> The attribute at the start of the "
"range to turn into a comment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:755
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>end_attribute</parameter> The attribute at end of the range to "
"turn into a comment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:758
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns whether start_attribute and end_attribute belongs to the same syntax "
"highlight system. If they do, it is sane."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:762
#, no-c-format
msgid "using canComment"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: advanced.docbook:763
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"if ( document.canComment( document.attribute(1,0), document.attribute"
"(5,0) ) ) {\n"
"    // 1,0 and 5,0 belongs to the same syntax highlighting system\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:769
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.clear(); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:770
#, no-c-format
msgid "Clears the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:774
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.commentStart( <parameter>uint attribute</parameter> ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:779
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>attribute</parameter> The attribute of the text for which to get "
"the commentStart string."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the string required to start a multiline comment for a text with "
"attribute, or an empty string if multiline comments are not supported for "
"that text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:789
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.commentMarker( <parameter>uint attribute</parameter> ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:794
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>attribute</parameter> The attribute of the text for which to get "
"the commentMarker string"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:797
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the string used to mark the rest of the line as a comment for a text "
"with attribute or an empty string if single line comments are not supported "
"for that text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:804
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.commentEnd( <parameter>uint attribute</parameter> ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:809
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>attribute</parameter> The attribute of the text for which to get "
"the commentEnd string"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:812
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the string required to end a multiline comment for a text with "
"attribute, or an empty string if multiline comments are not supported for "
"that text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:819
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.editBegin(); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:821
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Start an editing group. All actions done until the call of editEnd() will be "
"grouped as one undo-action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:827
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.editEnd(); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:829
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finish an editing group."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:834
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.highlightMode; [property:read only]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:836
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The name of the document's highlight mode, such as JavaScript or C++. If no "
"syntax highlight mode is set for the document, the value is None. Notice "
"that you need to use the English name in cases where it differs from the "
"translated one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:844
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.indentMode; [property:read only]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:846
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The name of the document indent mode, such as <literal>normal</literal> or "
"<literal>cstyle</literal>. Remember that if no indent mode is set, the value "
"is <literal>none</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:854
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.indentWidth; [property:read only]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:856
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The indentation width set for the document. This is used if space indenting "
"is enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:862
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"document.insertLine( <parameter>uint line</parameter>, <parameter>string "
"text</parameter> ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:867
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>line</parameter> document line number"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:869
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>text</parameter> text to insert"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:871
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Inserts a new line with the text <parameter>text</parameter> at the line "
"<parameter>line</parameter>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:877
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"document.insertText( <parameter>uint line</parameter>, <parameter>uint "
"column</parameter>, <parameter>string text</parameter> ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:883
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>line</parameter> the line number"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:884
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>column</parameter> the column"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:885
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>text</parameter> the text which is to be inserted"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:888
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Inserts the text <parameter>text</parameter> in line <parameter>line</"
"parameter> and column <parameter>column</parameter>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: advanced.docbook:894
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.length(); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:896
#, no-c-format
msgid "Returns the document's size in bytes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:901
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.lines(); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:903
#, no-c-format
msgid "Returns the number of lines in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: advanced.docbook:908
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.mixedIndent; [property:read only]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:910
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A boolean telling whether the mixed-indent setting is enabled for the "
"document. If so, indentation is optimized to contain a mix of tab characters "
"and spaces like used by the Emacs editor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: advanced.docbook:917
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.removeLine( <parameter>uint line</parameter> ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:921
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>line</parameter> line number"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:923
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removes the document line line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:928
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"document.removeText( <parameter>uint startLine</parameter>, <parameter>uint "
"startColumn</parameter>, <parameter>uint endLine</parameter>, "
"<parameter>uint endColumn</parameter> ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:934 advanced.docbook:997 advanced.docbook:1146
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>startLine</parameter> specifies the beginning line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:936 advanced.docbook:999 advanced.docbook:1147
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>startColumn</parameter> specifies the beginning column"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:938 advanced.docbook:1001 advanced.docbook:1148
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>endLine</parameter> specifies the ending line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:940 advanced.docbook:1003 advanced.docbook:1149
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>endColumn</parameter> specifies the ending column"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:943
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Removes the text range from line <parameter>startLine</parameter> and column "
"<parameter>startColumn</parameter> up to line <parameter>endLine</parameter> "
"and column <parameter>endColumn</parameter>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:951
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.setText( <parameter>string text</parameter> ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:956
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>text</parameter> document text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:958
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sets the entire document content to <parameter>text</parameter>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:963
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.spaceIndent; [property:read only]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:965
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A boolean telling whether space-indent is enabled for the document. If so, "
"the document is indented with indentWidth spaces per level, otherwise "
"indentation is one tab character per level."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:972
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.textFull(); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:974
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the full document text. If the text spans over multiple lines the "
"linefeed character is <constant>\\n</constant>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: function
#: advanced.docbook:980
#, no-c-format
msgid "document.textLine( uint line ); [function]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:984
#, no-c-format
